---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {releaseChords} from '../../data/chords.js';
import {createChord,prettyNote} from '../../lib/music.js';
const one=createChord(releaseChords[0]);const two=createChord(releaseChords[4]);
---
<BaseLayout title="Compare Piano Chords Side by Side | Piano Chord Explorer" description="Compare two piano chords by notes, shared tones and audio. Practice smooth chord transitions with a free side-by-side comparison tool." canonicalPath="/tools/chord-compare/" crumbs={[{name:'Chord Compare',href:'/tools/chord-compare/'}]}>
<div class="container page-hero tool-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Free interactive tool</span><h1>Two chords.<br/>One clear difference.</h1><p class="lead">See which notes your chords share, which notes move, and how each harmony sounds. Build a smoother piano chord transition. When you arrive from an individual lesson, both chords are already selected for you.</p></div>
<section class="container section-compact"><div class="tool-grid">
  <article class="panel compare-col"><label for="compare-a" class="input-label">First chord</label><select class="field" id="compare-a">{releaseChords.map(e=><option value={e.slug} selected={e.slug===one.slug}>{e.name}</option>)}</select><div id="compare-a-view" style="margin-top:18px"><h2>{one.name}</h2><p>{one.notes.map(prettyNote).join(' · ')}</p><img class="keyboard-image" src={`/diagrams/${one.slug}.svg`} alt={`${one.name} keyboard diagram`}/><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-play-midi={one.inversions[0].midi.join(',')}>▶ Play A</button></div></article>
  <article class="panel compare-col"><label for="compare-b" class="input-label">Second chord</label><select class="field" id="compare-b">{releaseChords.map(e=><option value={e.slug} selected={e.slug===two.slug}>{e.name}</option>)}</select><div id="compare-b-view" style="margin-top:18px"><h2>{two.name}</h2><p>{two.notes.map(prettyNote).join(' · ')}</p><img class="keyboard-image" src={`/diagrams/${two.slug}.svg`} alt={`${two.name} keyboard diagram`}/><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-play-midi={two.inversions[0].midi.join(',')}>▶ Play B</button></div></article>
</div><div id="compare-result" class="compare-result" aria-live="polite"><h3>Shared notes</h3><p>Pick two chords to compare their pitch classes and learn a simple note-moving exercise.</p></div></section>
<section class="container section-compact">
  <div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">PRACTICE THE TRANSITION</span><h2>Two real chord changes to try</h2><p>Use the selectors above to hear each pair. Then look for notes that can stay in the same place while just one voice moves.</p></div></div>
  <div class="two-col">
    <article class="panel prose"><h3>Bm → D major: keep two notes still</h3><p>B minor uses B–D–F♯. D major uses D–F♯–A. They share D and F♯, so one voice can change from B down to A while the other two remain. That makes a useful beginner exercise in economical voice leading.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/chord-compare/?a=b-minor&amp;b=d-major">Compare Bm and D major with the correct pair selected ↗</a></p><p><a class="text-link" href="/chords/b-minor/">Read the Bm practice lesson ↗</a></p></article>
    <article class="panel prose"><h3>C7 → Cmaj7: change only the seventh</h3><p>C7 uses C–E–G–B♭, while Cmaj7 uses C–E–G–B natural. Keep C, E and G in place and move B♭ up one semitone to B. The sound changes even though the root, third and fifth are identical.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/chord-compare/?a=c-7&amp;b=c-major-7">Compare C7 and Cmaj7 ↗</a></p><p><a class="text-link" href="/guides/seventh-chords-piano/">Learn the different seventh types ↗</a></p></article>
  </div>
  <p class="help-text">The compare tool checks the sounding pitch classes. For two chords in different octaves, the shortest physical finger movement may differ from the root-position diagrams. Use the <a href="/tools/inversion-explorer/">inversion explorer</a> to choose a comfortable voicing.</p>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
